{
  "run_id": "3fad0081a1",
  "final_message": "**Status:** Reproduced\n\n**Expected:** `<template #_slot1>` / `<template #_slot2>` content passed to `SubComponent` replaces the slot fallback content (the Vue 3.5.13 behavior).\n\n**Actual:** The fallback content is rendered (`default1|default2` instead of `one|two`). The same happens on published 3.5.14 and 3.5.17, and on the checked-out revision a9269c6.\n\n**Trigger:** A component whose slot names start with `_` (`<template #_slot1>`), used inside the default slot of a parent (`BaseLayout`) that also receives a conditional slot template (`<template v-if=\"show\" #header>`). Without the `v-if`, or with names that do not start with `_`, the output is correct (I checked all four combinations). One thing to know: I could not decode the playground link, because the sandbox denied it. The scenario is built from the report's written conditions, not the reporter's exact code.\n\n```\n<BaseLayout>\n  <template v-if=\"show\" #header>H</template>\n  <SubComponent>\n    <template #_slot1>one</template>\n    <template #_slot2>two</template>\n  </SubComponent>\n</BaseLayout>\n```\n\n`BaseLayout` is `<header><slot name=\"header\"/></header><main><slot/></main>`. `SubComponent` is `<div class=\"sub\"><slot name=\"_slot1\">default1</slot>|<slot name=\"_slot2\">default2</slot></div>`.\n\n**Run:** `pnpm vitest run packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` (exits 1 now).\n\n**Passes when:** The same spec run against published `vue@3.5.13` (aliased in a scratch vitest config under /tmp) passes with exit 0. Against `vue@3.5.14` it fails with the same message.\n\n**Likely cause (unconfirmed pointer):** With temporary logging (reverted), `SubComponent` gets its slots through `initSlots` with `optimized=false`. The `BaseLayout` default slot is rendered through the `v-if`-driven dynamic-slot path. `assignSlots` in `packages/runtime-core/src/componentSlots.ts` then skips keys that `isInternalKey` matches, and that matches every key starting with `_`, including `_slot1` and `_slot2`.\n\n**Artifacts:** `packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts` is the only change in the working tree. No production code was changed.\n",
  "run_command": "pnpm vitest run packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts",
  "patch": "diff --git a/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..5df3b7d\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/packages/vue/__tests__/slotUnderscoreName.spec.ts\n@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@\n+import { createApp, ref } from 'vue'\n+\n+// A slot outlet whose name starts with \"_\" must render the content passed via\n+// <template #_name>, even when the component using it sits next to a\n+// conditionally rendered (v-if) slot <template> of its parent component.\n+// Reported as a regression since v3.5.14 (worked in v3.5.13).\n+test('<template #_slot> content replaces fallback next to a v-if slot template', () => {\n+  const BaseLayout = {\n+    template: `<header><slot name=\"header\" /></header><main><slot /></main>`,\n+  }\n+  const SubComponent = {\n+    template: `<div class=\"sub\"><slot name=\"_slot1\">default1</slot>|<slot name=\"_slot2\">default2</slot></div>`,\n+  }\n+  const show = ref(true)\n+  const App = {\n+    setup: () => ({ show }),\n+    template: `\n+      <BaseLayout>\n+        <template v-if=\"show\" #header>H</template>\n+        <SubComponent>\n+          <template #_slot1>one</template>\n+          <template #_slot2>two</template>\n+        </SubComponent>\n+      </BaseLayout>`,\n+  }\n+  const app = createApp(App)\n+  app.component('BaseLayout', BaseLayout)\n+  app.component('SubComponent', SubComponent)\n+  const root = document.createElement('div')\n+  app.mount(root)\n+  expect(root.querySelector('.sub')!.textContent!.replace(/\\s/g, '')).toBe(\n+    'one|two',\n+  )\n+})\n"
}
